Determine the classification and taxonomic status of the Cypress and Ajuga genera within the botanical nomenclature system.
Based on general botanical knowledge, the classification and taxonomic status of the Cypress and Ajuga genera are as follows:

- Cypress (genus: Cupressus or Taxodium, depending on the species) is a genus of coniferous trees within the family Cupressaceae. It belongs to the order Cupressales and the class Pinopsida.

- Ajuga (also known as Bugleweed) is a genus of flowering plants within the family Lamiaceae (Mint family). It belongs to the order Lamiales and the class Magnoliopsida (Angiosperms).
