Based on the provided context, I found that the administrative division of the country that includes Hatton Hill and Hatton Castle, Angus, is a county. 

Historically, the UK was divided into counties or shires, which were administrative areas through which all civil responsibilities of the government were passed. Each county or shire had a county town as its administrative centre and was divided into individual parishes that were defined along ecclesiastic boundaries. 

However, between 1889 (1890 in Scotland) and 1974, the political boundaries were based on the traditional counties, but due to changes, the current administrative divisions of the UK are different. 

