What was the primary cause of the military conflict between the British Raj and the Emirate of Afghanistan from 1878 to 1880?
The primary cause of the military conflict between the British Raj and the Emirate of Afghanistan from 1878 to 1880 was the British attempt to limit Russian influence in Afghanistan, as well as quell raiding from across the border, following the arrival of Russian envoys in Kabul on 22 July 1878.
